.TH ZONAR_SRV 8
.SH NAME
zonar_srv \- zonar server to inspect a file system use of zoned devices

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zonar_srv
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR...] \fIpath\fP

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zonar_srv
provides a server to allow \fBzonar\fP(8) to remotely inspect and display the
use of the blockgroups of a zoned filesystem. \fIpath\fP must specify
the mount directory of the file system to inspect, and must be specified after
all options.

By default, \fBzonar_srv\fP listens for client connections. With the
\fR\-\-connect\fP option, \fBzonar_srv\fP instead connects to a \fBzonar\fP
client started with the \fR\-\-listen\fP option (reverse connection mode).

\fBzonar_srv\fP requires root privileges to access the device information.
When \fBzonar\fP is used to inspect a local file system,
\fBzonar_srv\fP is automatically started by \fBzonar\fP using
\fBpkexec\fP(1), and does not need to be started manually.

Currently \fBzonar_srv\fP supports the XFS and btrfs file systems.

.SH OPTIONS
\fBzonar_srv\fP options are as follows.
.TP
.BR \-\-help,\ \-h
Display a command line help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-verbose,\ \-v
Enable verbose mode (for debugging).
.TP
.BR \-\-version,\ \-V
Display \fBzonar_srv\fP version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-connect,\ \-c\ \fIipaddr\fP
Reverse connection mode: instead of waiting for a client connection, connect to
the client at the specified IP address.
.TP
.BR \-\-port,\ \-p\ \fIport\fP
Specify the port number to listen for client connections on, or to connect to
the client on when the \fR\-\-connect\fP option is used. The default port is
49152.

